# Decompose before building

Do not dump a whole page into one file. Break work until each piece has a single job.

## UI

- **Page** (`app/`) — compose sections, pass data and callbacks.
- **Section** — one band of the Figma screen (hero, filters, match grid).
- **Card / control** — one reusable unit (match card, invite button, signature pad).
- Extract a component when JSX repeats, when a block maps 1:1 to a Figma frame, or when it would be useful on another route.
- Compose for a **phone** width first; add breakpoints only if specified.

## Features

Ship in slices, for example: catalogs → listing form → match cards → invite → agreement text → drawn signature. Each slice should compile and look complete before the next.

## Logic

- Matching, agreement drafting, and mock lookups live in `lib/` (pure functions), not inside JSX.
- Keep functions small; name them after the slice (`getPerfectMatches`, `draftSkillAgreement`).
